 "title": "Goal line and short yardage: why a different back scores the touchdowns",
 "html": "<p><strong>The situation:</strong> the ball is on the 1, 2 or 3-yard line, or it's 3rd/4th and 1 anywhere. The offense needs a yard or two, and the defense knows it.</p>\n<p><strong>Both teams pack in.</strong> The offense brings in extra blockers: two tight ends and a fullback (\"22 personnel,\" Lesson 1). The defense answers with eight or nine players crowded near the line (a \"heavy box,\" Lesson 2), because there's no deep field left to protect (Lesson 12).</p>\n<div class=\"diagram\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 260\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Goal-line formation: two tight ends, a fullback and a power back against eight defenders packed near the line, with the power back running into the A gap\"><defs><marker id=\"m17w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"44\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.12)\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"700\">END ZONE</text><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"400\" y1=\"44\" y2=\"44\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"6\" y=\"58\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.85)\">goal line</text><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"400\" y1=\"120\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"6\" y=\"115\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.85)\">ball on the 2</text><rect x=\"108\" y=\"62\" width=\"196\" height=\"54\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"rgba(242,183,5,.10)\" stroke=\"#F2B705\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"56\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#F2B705\" font-weight=\"700\">9 defenders packed in the box</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"105\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"108.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"178\" cy=\"105\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"178\" y=\"108.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"105\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"108.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"234\" cy=\"105\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"234\" y=\"108.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"105\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"108.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"100\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"103.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">DL</text><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"78\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"165\" y=\"81.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">LB</text><circle cx=\"247\" cy=\"78\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"81.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">LB</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"92\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"95.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">CB</text><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"92\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"95.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">CB</text><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"74\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"206\" y=\"77.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">S</text><circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"78\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#F2B705\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"81.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\">S</text><rect x=\"140\" y=\"124\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"166\" y=\"124\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"192\" y=\"124\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"218\" y=\"124\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"244\" y=\"124\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"133\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"136.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">TE</text><circle cx=\"284\" cy=\"133\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"284\" y=\"136.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">TE</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"160\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"163.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">QB</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"188\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"191.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">FB</text><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"218\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"202\" y=\"221.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">RB</text><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"150\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"153.5\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F4D31\">WR</text><path d=\"M191 210 Q 172 168 189 125 L 189 34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" marker-end=\"url(#m17w)\"/><text x=\"189\" y=\"148\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#14202B\" font-weight=\"700\"></text><text x=\"394\" y=\"168\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"700\">2 tight ends + fullback:</text><text x=\"394\" y=\"181\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#fff\">extra blockers (\"22\")</text><text x=\"222\" y=\"222\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" font-weight=\"700\">power back</text><text x=\"222\" y=\"235\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\">runs into the A gap</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"254\" font-family=\"Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"rgba(255,255,255,.85)\">No room to run around anyone: the play is about pushing 2 yards straight ahead.</text></svg></div>\n<p class=\"note\">White = offense, yellow = defense. White squares = offensive linemen. Dashed yellow box = the 9 defenders near the line. The arrow is the power back's run straight into the A gap (Lesson 14), the space next to the center.</p>\n<p><strong>Why a different back:</strong> near the goal line, speed matters less, because there's no open field to outrun anyone. What matters is <strong>power</strong> (pushing a pile forward), <strong>ball security</strong> (a fumble here costs 7 points), and <strong>fresh legs</strong>. Many teams use a bigger \"goal-line back\" for these carries and save their star for the open field.</p>\n<p><strong>Monday's example:</strong> Bijan Robinson (the explosive back) scored from 59 yards on his first carry. But <strong>Brian Robinson Jr.</strong> (the bigger back) got the goal-line work: 3 touchdowns from close range, including two from the 4. That split is why Bijan finished at 145 yards and 2 TDs instead of more, and why the 160+ bet missed.</p>\n<p><strong>Connecting the dots:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Play-action again (Lesson 16):</strong> because defenses expect a run here, goal-line play-action to a tight end is one of the most common touchdown plays in football.</li>\n  <li><strong>Quarterback sneaks:</strong> on 3rd or 4th and 1, many teams just have the QB push forward behind the center. It's the highest-success short-yardage play.</li>\n  <li><strong>Gaps (Lesson 14):</strong> with eight defenders in the box, every gap is filled. The offense wins only by moving bodies backward, which is why the biggest linemen matter most here.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Why it matters for betting:</strong> for a running back's <em>touchdown</em> or very high <em>yardage</em> props, check who gets carries inside the 5-yard line, not just who gets the most carries. A star back who shares goal-line work is a better bet for yards than for touchdowns.</p>\n<p><strong>Watch for it this weekend:</strong> when a team reaches the 3, note who comes on the field. Two tight ends and a fullback? Watch which back lines up deepest. That's who the coach trusts with the ball.</p>\n<p><strong>Video:</strong> search YouTube for \"NFL goal line offense explained\" or \"tush push explained.\"</p>",
